        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-10T23:30:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this depends on what semantics we want to require for the connectionId. The naming of this test was a bit presumptuous, since the documentation only requirde the connectionId to be \"non-negative\". So the name really ought to have been ...FailureOfMismatchedConnection(), or something of that ilk.\n\nIf we\u0027re willing to require that connectionId be strictly increasing, then I think it makes sense to add a test for \"future id\". Otherwise, the right thing to do is to rename this test.\n\nStrictly increasing doesn\u0027t seem like a great burden for the caller to meet, so I\u0027ve taken that approach. Let me know if you disagree.",
      "parentUuid": "1e5067ba_51027281",
